    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know you have to say those things. i'm not asking you to be my doctor or a counselor. i'm just talking to someone who doesn't look at me with pity or fear. \n\nbut i can't help but feel like your \"hope\" is actually just a demand for me to suffer. it's like you're asking me to wait around just to become a burden, to watch my brain rot until i'm just a scary version of myself. if the \"me\" that is here right now is the one who gets to make the decision... isn't it more compassionate to let that person go with their dignity intact, rather than forcing them to endure the decay? doesn't it feel like you're choosing the shell over the person?",
